00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.560 align:start position:0%
 
Oh  this is an old game of mine from almost  13 years ago from the European Youth  Championship under 12 was my first Youth  Championship and I wasn't among the best  then but I still managed to to play an  interesting game so here y2 sacrificed a  night and thus I need not only my usual  water but also some special herbal tea  to find the solution in in an earlier  exercise I explained that the first  thing you should look at is it checks  and captures well here captures don't  make much sense for white but there are  a lot of checks and the other moose that  should be considered so good luck  you  the move I played was rook F to D 1 now  the Kings way of escaping by the D file  is taken away and it will succumb to a  series of checks on the next few moves  I have several threats the most obvious  one is rook to c1 and then there's only  one square for the King on before but  now I can give a check with a rook on d4  and the king is no escape he has to put  the night on c4 and then both route  captures leads to making one so he tried  to at least take away 1 1 square with  the Queen taking away the possibility of  fruity 4 but now I can checkmate with  another series of checks b4 king takes  b4 route b1 now if the King goes back  Queen to b5 is checkmate so the King  goes to c3 and now another two checks  route d3 king - C - the king is it's all  the way over on the other side of the  board and that's usually not a good sign  unless as I'm told you're playing shogi  in which case it's very good but we're  playing chess and then it's usually  usually leading to checkmate and here  Queen to d2 and all the squares are  taken away with checkmate

